      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Constant Initialization (`ft_log.h`)** `constexpr const char* kLogTag` works, but modern C++ style prefers `inline constexpr` for header-defined string constants to prevent One Definition Rule (ODR) violations and duplicate string literals across translation units.\n\n* **Fix:** `inline constexpr std::string_view kLogTag \u003d \"focaltech\";`",
      "range": {
